    "problem_statement": "After the apps test change updates the ostest programs so that `testing/ostest/roundrobin.c` and `testing/ostest/spinlock.c` call `atomic_add` and use `atomic_read`, building the affected tests against the current NuttX kernel fails. The observed symptom is a link-time error, for example an undefined reference to `atomic_add` in `roundrobin.c`, such as `/roundrobin.c:137:(.text.get_primes_thread+0x128): undefined reference to 'atomic_add'`. The updated `roundrobin` code uses `atomic_add` to update a shared index, and the updated `spinlock` code uses `atomic_add` and `atomic_read` on a shared barrier. With the current kernel, `rr_test` and `spinlock_test` do not link, so they cannot be built or run. The required behavior is that, with the updated test programs, `rr_test` and `spinlock_test` build successfully and pass without modifying the test sources.",
